# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. NEVER remove these two lines.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
config/youtube_oauth.json
config/youtube_token.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Big binary files. Git is bad at these; they get uploaded as build artifacts
# instead (see .github/workflows/).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Unanchored, `output/` would
# match runs/<id>/output/ too - and because git never descends into an excluded
# directory, the `!runs/*/output/...` exceptions below could never take effect.
/audio/
/output/
/assets/stock/
/assets/charts/
/assets/music/
runs/*/audio/
runs/*/assets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A run's text files ARE committed, and that matters.
#
# The runs/ folder is the only memory this system has. Every chat message
# arrives in a brand-new container that knows nothing about the last one, so
# state.json, the topic list, the script and the metadata have to be in the
# repo or the conversation forgets itself between messages. They're small -
# a whole run is well under 200 KB of text.
#
# What must NOT be committed is the heavy output: one run held a 146 MB WAV,
# past GitHub's 100 MB file limit. So the output folder is excluded except for
# the three small files you'd want to read on your phone, and the binary
# extensions are blocked outright wherever they turn up.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/*/output/*
!runs/*/output/subtitles.srt
!runs/*/output/UPLOAD.md
!runs/*/output/description.txt

runs/**/*.wav
runs/**/*.mp3
runs/**/*.mp4
runs/**/*.webm
runs/**/*.mov
runs/**/*.jpg
runs/**/*.jpeg
runs/**/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed dependencies and caches - anyone can regenerate these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
frame.jpg

# Remotion build output and staged assets
remotion/public/
remotion/out/
remotion/build/

# Thumbnail bake-off output (tools/thumbnail_bakeoff.py). Throwaway comparison
# images and the answer key - no reason to commit them.
bakeoff/
runs/selftest/assets/
runs/selftest/output/
